      "title": "LOWER and UPPER: converting string case",
      "eyebrow": "Let's review",
      "lede": "LOWER converts to all lower case; UPPER converts to all upper case.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_sql_text_dates_casts.r01.p1",
          "text": "LOWER(text) converts every character in the string to lower case: LOWER('LAGOS') → 'lagos', LOWER('Lagos') → 'lagos'. UPPER(text) converts every character to upper case: UPPER('lagos') → 'LAGOS'. These functions are useful when city names or other categorical values were entered with inconsistent casing and you need to compare or group them reliably.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
