      "title": "Date subtraction gives elapsed days",
      "eyebrow": "Let's review",
      "lede": "Subtracting two dates returns the number of days between them.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_sql_text_dates_casts.r03.p1",
          "text": "Subtracting one date from another in SQL produces the number of days elapsed between them as an integer. If order_date is '2024-02-03' and you subtract '2024-01-01', the result is 33 days. This is different from EXTRACT, which pulls a single subfield (year, month, day) out of one date value.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
