      "type": "remediation",
      "concept_ids": [
        "sql.date_time_functions"
      ],
      "title": "EXTRACT and date subtraction",
      "eyebrow": "Let's review",
      "lede": "EXTRACT pulls a subfield from one date; subtraction gives days between two dates.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_sql_text_dates_casts.r04.p1",
          "text": "EXTRACT(field FROM source) retrieves a single subfield from a date, time, timestamp, or interval value. The field can be year, month, day, hour, minute, second, and others. EXTRACT(month FROM order_date) returns the month number (1–12) for each order. To get the number of days between two dates, subtract them directly: order_date - '2024-01-01' gives elapsed days.",
